 "text": "Our attention is pulled in many directions every day. Messages arrive, alarms ring and tabs multiply on the screen. To do focused work, I protect blocks of time. I choose one task and set a timer for forty minutes. During that time, I shut my email and put my phone in another room. If a new idea appears, I write it on a note and return to the task. When the timer ends, I take a short break. Most days, I manage three of these blocks. That is often enough to finish the work that matters. Protecting your attention is one of the most useful skills you can build at work."
